    "explanation": "Both of you are broadly right about the main thing, and the $4.00 comes back.\n\nTo the rider: the no-show fee cannot stand. A cancellation fee is chargeable only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold, and here three fail. (d) fails first: the trip was terminated by the driver with reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which the policy treats as the driver's own admission that he could not find you - it is expressly not one of the three no-show codes. (b) and (c) also fail: the GPS trace contains no qualifying in-radius fix at all (closest recorded approach 284.95 m against the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius), and the in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second minimum. Your own track shows you were at the pin the whole time - 31 fixes, all stationary, never more than 22.5 m away.\n\nBecause the driver held position about 285 m from the pin - outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside the 400 m ceiling - this is a wrong-approach case under POL-NS-03, not a rider no-show. The cancellation fee is refunded to you in full: $4.00.\n\nTo the driver: you waited almost seven minutes and did nothing wrong beyond ending up at the wrong kerb, so the cost does not fall on you. Neither party named an entrance, block, tower or bay anywhere in the chat, and this venue has four registered pickup points. Under POL-NS-03(ii) the mislocation is therefore attributed to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and you receive a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50% of the fee - $2.00 - charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. The 80% no-show compensation of $3.20 under POL-NS-07 is not payable because it requires the no-show charge to be valid in the first place and it is not, as you acknowledged. The $4.00 refund to the rider and the $2.00 payment to you are independent and are not set off against each other.\n\nOn the evidence. The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00206) is impaired at weight 0.8 for LOW_SAMPLE_RATE (median 18 s against a nominal 10 s cadence). That is a schema-level tag only: the trace has no gap over 120 s, 52 fixes across the window, the rider track present and no clock skew, so it meets none of the integrity limbs (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08, it does not require escalation, and the distances it reports survive the discount. It does, however, cap confidence at 0.8, which is still above the 0.70 floor. The rider's POL-NS-04 argument (unanswered contact) cannot run, because the chat holds only two SYSTEM messages and no rider locating message; that does not change the outcome. The traffic-advisory/waiting-period route under POL-NS-06 is not reached, POL-NS-03 already producing the full refund. POL-NS-05 produces no false-arrival referral: the arrival marker was set 284.95 m from the pin - inside the 300 m line - and the stationary fixes are at 0.0 km/h. No escalation applies: confidence is above the floor, no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or presence in a way no clause resolves, there are no repeat counterparty disputes, the anti-farming check is not tripped (1 no-show termination in 30 days against 187 completed trips), and the only impairment is schema-level."
